WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.362
Why does this need code?

2
00:00:01.362 --> 00:00:05.099
The organizational unit (OU)
tree scoped Group Policy,

3
00:00:05.099 --> 00:00:08.326
and Group Policy
inheritance retires with it.

4
00:00:08.326 --> 00:00:12.075
So every GPO setting has to
land somewhere on purpose.

5
00:00:12.075 --> 00:00:18.153
Gate 0 splits every GPO by track,
and its Validate step runs VK-INT-07,

6
00:00:18.153 --> 00:00:25.225
to show which GPOs Group Policy analytics
has imported and how ready they are.

7
00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:28.763
Gate 5 moves each setting
to exactly one owner.

8
00:00:28.763 --> 00:00:33.362
And Gate 8 cuts over by disabling
GPO links, never deleting them.

9
00:00:33.362 --> 00:00:38.137
Moving Group Policy to Intune
changes the baseline of every device.

10
00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:42.036
This module is the code between
those gates: a plan per setting,

11
00:00:42.036 --> 00:00:46.920
a library of reviewed files, and a sync
that creates only what a dry run showed.
